It is Sunday evening.
The doorbell rings.
Moti runs to the door.
He wags his tail very fast.
I open the door.
Asha is standing outside.
Moti jumps happily on her.
"Moti, sit down!" Asha tells him.
"Maya, how was the weekend?" she asks.
"It was very good," I say.
I give Asha his leash and bowls.
"Take these," I tell her.
"Moti was a very good guest."
"But he likes sandals a lot."
I show Asha my sandal.
"He chewed it a little yesterday," I say, laughing.
"Oh no, I am so sorry!" Asha says.
"Oh, it is no problem," I smile.
"Moti, chewing shoes is forbidden!"
Asha scolds him.
"You must chew only your toy," she tells him.
"Thank you for the help, Maya," she says.
"Bring him here again," I say.
